  "term": "equipment design",
  "definition": "Equipment design is the development of protective gear and its testing standards using measured information about how physical forces act on the body. In this source, it refers specifically to using current-distribution data from simulated lightning strikes to guide the design and evaluation of personal lightning protection equipment.",
